# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Rework environment variables — copy this file to ".env" and fill in values.
#   cp .env.example .env
# Every integration Rework uses is FREE. You can run the app with none of
# these set; they just unlock extra food-search sources and photo scanning.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# USDA FoodData Central — free personal key (~2 min):
#   https://fdc.nal.usda.gov/api-key-signup.html
#
# In a real deployment, USDA search runs through the api/usda-search.js proxy
# (which fixes a browser CORS block). The proxy reads USDA_API_KEY (preferred,
# server-side) OR VITE_USDA_API_KEY. Set USDA_API_KEY in your HOST's env vars:
#   USDA_API_KEY=your_key_here
#
# The VITE_-prefixed version below is a client-exposed fallback for static-only
# deploys with no serverless functions (may still be CORS-blocked). Leave blank
# to simply skip USDA results (Open Food Facts + your local library still work).
VITE_USDA_API_KEY=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# GEMINI_API_KEY is used ONLY by the backend serverless function
# (api/analyze-food.js) for photo food scanning. Get a free key at
#   https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
#
# Do NOT put a real value here for a normal `npm run dev` — this key must stay
# SERVER-SIDE ONLY. Set it in your hosting dashboard's environment variables
# (Vercel: Project Settings > Environment Variables), NOT prefixed with VITE_.
# The only time it belongs in a local .env is when testing the function with
# `vercel dev` (never with plain `npm run dev`, which doesn't run /api).
#
# Note: barcode scanning does NOT need this key — it works with no setup.
# GEMINI_API_KEY=
